	if(kind=="mesh_wall_opening") return R"json({"workflow":["get_object(target_uid)","validate_mesh(uid=target_uid)","build_mesh(cutter) with one closed box or cylinder positioned in world space so it fully crosses the wall","validate_mesh(uid=cutter_uid)","boolean_mesh(replace_uid=target_uid, operand_uid=cutter_uid, operation=subtract); this consumes the cutter","validate_mesh(uid=target_uid)","get_object(target_uid) and render_view from front and side"],"notes":["Use this sequence for a real opening in an existing native .bmesh wall, floor, roof or furniture object.","The target and cutter must be closed manifold meshes and each must be at most 16384 triangles for boolean_mesh. The server maps the cutter from its world transform into the target's local space, so do not guess target-local coordinates twice.","Do not replace the target with a new generic cube. boolean_mesh retains the target UID and material slots, consumes the cutter after success, and leaves both source objects unchanged when validation or the Boolean fails.","If validate_mesh reports an open/nonmanifold target, a non-native model, a missing server resource or more than 16384 triangles, read the exact error. For supported non-native formats use convert_mesh; for dense meshes use deliberate simplify_mesh then validate again. Do not automatically replace the shape with voxels or a generic approximation."],"tool_sequence_only":true})json";
